Peter wrote:
> OK, I've got a little Human Tourist going, 0.0.7E7, no real armor or 
> weapons to speak of, though he's got a bag of holding, in the non-Mines 
> market with two kitties. Plenty of cash on hand, so he bought a blessed 
> magic lamp. Assuming he gets a wish, what should he ask for? I'm tempted 
> to wait until he clears Sokoban to decide, but dying holding a magic 
> lamp is just too bogus. I'm thinking either grey or silver dragon scale 
> mail. Any advice or personal preferences?

You need magic protection and a good weapon.  So why not wish for 
Magicbane?  Because it does not boost the damage you deal too much, it 
will not make you overconfident.  It can help with survival by Engraving 
as well.

Good armor alone will not save you, a good weapon alone will not save 
you either.  Magicbane is a decent compromise (if you don't mind wishing 
for artifacts).

After Sokoban, if that does not yield the amulet, I would rather wish 
for silver dragon scale mail.  But I also think the wish should be spent 
immediately, since you don't have a fighter going.
